            <ArticleTitle>Rh-Catalyzed Conversion of 3-Diazoindolin-2-imines to 5H-Pyrazino[2,3-b]indoles with Photoluminescent Properties.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6514-6517</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03211</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rhodium-catalyzed reaction between 3-diazoindolin-2-imines and 2H-azirines, followed by treatment with a base, furnishes 5H-pyrazino[2,3-b]indoles in excellent yields. A number of functional groups tolerate the reaction conditions, and the resulting 5H-pyrazino[2,3-b]indoles present strong photoluminecence in solutions, powders, and films.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
